                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had this game on the Wii when I was younger but the controls were so horrendous I never really played it. I was surprised to find it on Steam for less than a dollar. Initially on windows the contrast was so bad I could not play it but it seems to run on SteamOS flawlessly. \n\nSo this game is not very good, the physics are arcade-y, there are only 8 tracks (16 if you count the reverse ones). I beat the game in less than an hour. There are also only 3 weapons (mines, rockets and primary). \n\nThe game functions fine as a kart racer, but is super fast-paced. The entire story is just 4 race tournaments. There are a few challenges as well to unlock new cars. \n\nThe biggest pro of this game is the soundtrack. The music is unique and fits well within the design of the game.\n\nIf you like flash-style battle racers you may enjoy this for an hour, but I would def get it on sale for less than a dollar. I just do not understand how this game never got fleshed out more with so many people working on it. This feels more like an alpha game content wise.",
